            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "40°F is the upper limit, so a fridge reading 40°F is just inside the line, with no margin. Because the inside temperature rises every time the door opens, a fridge sitting at 40°F will spend part of the day above it. Turn the control one step colder, wait 24 hours, and re-check until you see about 37°F."
